{"t": 14831, "msg": {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch9tX1pjFxeRW8BPKthkA", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I read the whole file and found no serious bugs, only a handful of small ones.\n\nThe most real one is in the replay function. If the newest exchange alone is longer than the character limit, the loop breaks at once and returns an empty string. The backend then gets no history at all, instead of a truncated version of the newest turn.\n\nDelete has a related gap. If a chat file is already gone but its index entry remains, delete returns false without cleaning the index. That ghost entry can never be removed from the list, except by the prune command or an index rebuild.\n\nExport can crash with a traceback. If the folder doesn't exist, or another process grabs the same filename between the exists check and the exclusive open, the resulting OSError isn't caught in main. The CLI then prints a traceback instead of an error message.\n\nTwo minor things. Rebuilding a damaged index loses the record of which chat each agent is in, and it leaves the list unsorted until the next save. Also, the meta builder assumes every exchange is a dict, so one malformed exchange in a file would break the listing.\n\nI haven't changed anything. I can fix the replay and delete cases and add tests for them if you like."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 9380, "cache_read_input_tokens": 25172, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 9380}, "output_tokens": 3, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "169cf839-2d38-4673-935c-5c40c76dff78", "uuid": "009c0cc3-003a-4990-8864-0a35a589e015", "tim